    "perplexity": {
      "description": "Free Peace Sweet is the third studio album by Dodgy, released in 1996 on A&M Records. It found the band at the height of the Britpop era, pairing bright, melodic songwriting with a more polished pop-rock and indie-rock sound; the album also drew influence from artists as varied as Beastie Boys, Crosby, Stills & Nash, and Dr. John.\n\nThe record became Dodgy’s biggest commercial success, reaching No. 7 on the UK Albums Chart and later earning platinum certification from the BPI. Its singles helped define the album’s profile, especially “Good Enough,” which became the band’s highest-charting single, alongside “In a Room,” “If You’re Thinking of Me,” and “Found You.”",
